%description:
Tests a locked receive buffer that runs out of room, as Linux ICSK_ACK_NOMEM.
The server application does not read (autoRead=false), and the client sends
two segments of 1000 bytes. At t=1.5 s the server application sets SO_RCVBUF to
1000 bytes, less than the 2000 bytes in its queue. The third segment (A005)
does not fit: the server drops it and offers a zero window, although its last
offer was 14384 bytes. The server also refuses the retransmission A006 with a
zero window. At t=4 s the application reads the queue. The ACK of the next
retransmission (B006) offers 437 bytes: the empty buffer at the truesize ratio
of the received segments (112/256). The offer is less than one MSS, but it is
the whole buffer, so the receiver SWS rule does not hold it back.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

sim-time-limit = 20s
*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 2000; 2.0 1000"
*.*_tcp.mss = 1000
*.cli_tcp.nagleEnabled = false
*.srv_app.autoRead=false
*.srv_app.rcvBufScript="1.5 1000"
*.srv_app.readScript="4.0 10000"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[2.001 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A 2001:3001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[2.003 B004] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 2001 win 0 
[3.001 A006] A.1000 > B.2000: A 2001:3001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[3.003 B005] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 2001 win 0 
[5.001 A007] A.1000 > B.2000: A 2001:3001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[5.003 B006] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 2001 win 437 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
SO_RCVBUF: the receive buffer is 1000 bytes, locked
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
RcvQueueBuffer has run out, dropping segment
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
